# Element Geometry Contract

The most error-prone part of adding or changing shapes: **rendering and hit-testing must use identical vertices**.

## Pipeline

```
getXPoints (bounds.ts)     → roughjs polygon (shape.ts) → canvas + SVG export
deconstructXElement (utils.ts) → collision, distance, bounds line-segments
getPolygonShape (utils/shape.ts) → export polygon helpers
```

If these diverge, the shape **draws correctly but is not clickable where it appears** — the classic demo bug in `seed-demo-bug` bug A.

## Rules

- When adding shape `X`, add **both** `getXPoints` and `deconstructXElement`; model on `diamond`
- Never "simplify" corner math in only one of bounds vs utils
- `getElementAbsoluteCoords` reuses `x/y/width/height` for bounding-box shapes — no change needed if using that model
- After geometry edits, run `yarn test:typecheck` — `assertNever` in `shape.ts` and `typeChecks.ts` catches missing switch cases

## Quick audit

For any shape type, grep these files for the type string and confirm all branches exist:

- `packages/element/src/bounds.ts`
- `packages/element/src/utils.ts`
- `packages/element/src/shape.ts`
- `packages/element/src/collision.ts`
- `packages/element/src/distance.ts`
- `packages/utils/src/shape.ts`

Use the `geometry-auditor` subagent for a structured read-only review.
